fact WorkItem(id: "WI-382", description: some(value: "DESIGN (long-horizon): UNIFICATION AS A FRAMEWORK OF PER-SORT REGISTERED ALGORITHMS. Stub proposal: docs/proposals/future/unification-framework.md. Unification is not one fixed algorithm but a framework that dispatches to a per-sort REGISTERED algorithm, syntactic (first-order) as the default; a sort may register its own -- effect rows register row unification (Remy; WI-307, delivered), sets register AC, intervals register CLP(R). CONDENSES three otherwise-separate concerns into one mechanism (docs/design/type-parameter-scoping.md sec.'Relationship to the logical-rules engine'): effects stop being a parallel algebra (just the sort whose registered unifier IS the row algorithm); value-in-type (denoted) equality (Modify[c1] vs Modify[c2]) is the embedded value's sort's unifier; the resolver's term unify and the typer's unify_types become a SHARED dispatcher (the 'two unifications' is then implementation, not a definitional gap). DEFINITIONAL WORK to extend the stub: (1) the unifier interface a sort registers (unify_S(a,b,store)->store?; monad subclass) + the value-equality it induces; (2) theory COMPOSITION when a term mixes theories (Nelson-Oppen / Baader-Schulz combination of unification algorithms; decidable under disjoint-signature conditions order-sorted anthill largely meets); (3) termination obligation per theory + combination; (4) discrimination-tree indexing under non-syntactic theories (AC indexing is harder). FORMAL BASIS + Scala prototype: R.S.Shevchenko, A.Yu.Doroshenko, O.A.Yatsenko, 'Embedding a family of logic languages with reprogrammable monadic unification in Scala', Problems in Programming (Problemy Prohramuvannia) 2024 No.1, DOI 10.15407/pp2024.01.03 (monadic unification = theories as monad subclasses = this framework). This is the SUBSTRATE that WI-010 (resolver-as-type-checker = typing-as-constraints = CLP) wants; effects (WI-307) are the existing proof-of-concept. Long-horizon; not on the critical path (WI-379->WI-368). ACCEPTANCE: design only for now (extend the stub to a numbered proposal); promotion = assign a main-sequence proposal number + move out of future/."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-010"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-382", author: "user", content: "ORDER-RELATION SCOPE (join/meet) — concrete deferred item from WI-293: the variance-aware join_types PARAMETERIZED-LUB construction. Today join_types (kb/typing.rs) only ever RETURNS one input or widens the nominal side up the lattice — it never CONSTRUCTS a type, so join(Option[T=Cat], Option[T=Dog]) gives a conservative common supertype, not the strict lub Option[T=Animal]. Building the real lub is the ORDER relation this framework subsumes (variance is the order relation, sibling of unification/equality, already SLD-rules-over-Covariant/Contravariant-facts — see expansion-during-unification.md sec8 \"Variance ... enriches the WI-382 destination\"). Per-parameter recipe: covariant param => join(av,bv); invariant => require av==bv; CONTRAVARIANT => meet(av,bv) — and MEET DOES NOT EXIST yet, which is precisely why this lands in the per-sort ORDERING framework (join AND meet as registered per-sort order ops, not just unify). WI-293 delivered the SUBTYPING half (variance-aware parameterized_compatible, the soundness primitive); this lub/join+meet half is deferred here. Not on the critical path (WI-379->WI-380).", at: "2026-06-04T13:46:03Z")

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-382", name: "typing")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-382", author: "user", content: "CORRECTION (concrete join/meet pulled out to WI-464): the variance-aware join_types PARAMETERIZED-LUB + meet_types is now its OWN near-term WI (WI-464), depends ONLY on WI-293 (delivered) — NOT on this item or WI-010. Rationale: the typer is term-backed Rust (join_types/declared_variance/parameterized_compatible_view all in kb/typing.rs), and the WI-293 subtyping half proved you build the order-relation ops directly in Rust without the per-sort registered-algorithm substrate. The earlier 'deferred from WI-293, lands here' framing over-coupled: it turned a CONCEPTUAL kinship (variance/join/meet = the order relation, sibling of unification) into an IMPLEMENTATION dependency, via the false 'meet does not exist => need the framework' leap (meet_types is just join_types's dual over the same lattice). WI-382 REMAINS the eventual generalization HOME: when this framework lands, join_types/meet_types (built in WI-464) fold into registered per-sort ordering ops — a future refactor target, not a blocker for the LUB.", at: "2026-06-14T17:01:48Z")
